// GEN_RFX_Reflex.c  (GENERATED by analysis/harness/generator.py from the spec; edit the spec, not this file)
//
// PURPOSE:  Batch harness RFX. Feeds synthetic inputs through ReflexCore (13 variants:
//           L14, L20, L21, L30, NCL [info], NCA [control], NC2 [control], NC1 [control], NCH [control], NCK [control], NCW [control], NCS [control], NCT [control]) and writes the RAW outputs. It does NOT judge anything.
//           Python (analysis/harness/checker.py) measures and writes PASS/FAIL.
// PREREG:   analysis/harness/specs/RFX_ArticleFidelity.toml (this file)
// INPUTS:   Synthetic only, from the bar counter n: flat | level+amp*sin(2*pi*n/T), T=5,10,20,40,100 | alt level+amp*(-1)^n | ramp level+slope*n
//           level=11/10 amp=1/100 slope=1/10000. (b, H1 run 1) Decimal literals are float32 in this Zorro
//           build and the PI macro is 3.14159, so every constant is built at run time from integers.
//           EUR/USD is used only as a bar clock; clock_close is exported for the checker's magnitude guard.
// OUTPUT:   Data/GEN_RFX_raw.csv  (3000 rows n=0..2999 + header; 340 columns; values printed with 15 decimals)
//           copies sc (level 11/10 amp 1/10), of (level 22/10 amp 1/100): every sine again with the transform's level/amp (sc/of ...), for variants with invariance.
// CALLS:    144 filter calls per bar, variant-major, unconditional, fixed order (gotchas 3.1).
// FEEDING:  every x[n], n=0..2999, reaches the filters exactly once; INITRUN and EXITRUN feed and write nothing.
// NO LOOKBACK GUARD: LookBack = 0, warmup bars are exported too; the checker requires n = 0..2999 contiguous.
// SOURCES:  expected values and tolerances are in the spec, each with an (a)/(b)/(c) label.
//           Pattern copied from strategies/tests/H1_SuperSmoother2Pole_Harness.c (b: H1 run 2 PASS).
// Y[] slots: variant-major; per call the outputs in the listed order (the last is the return value); see the call comments.

#include <default.c>
